Add an application callback deciding when multi-line input is complete.

Upstream isocline accepts the input as soon as enter is pressed, unless the
line happens to end with the multiline_eol character ('\\'). A REPL needs to
decide completeness by its own rules instead -- clox continues input until a
blank line terminates the block.

This adds ic_set_is_complete(fun, arg). When a callback is set and multi-line
input is enabled, an enter that would have accepted an input the callback
calls incomplete inserts a newline and keeps editing. With no callback set the
behaviour is exactly as before. The existing multiline_eol path is untouched
and still takes precedence.

Kept deliberately generic (the policy lives in the application, not here) so
it can be offered upstream as-is.

Upstream: https://github.com/daanx/isocline at tag v1.1.0
Apply with: git apply -p1  # from clox/vendor/isocline/

--- a/include/isocline.h
+++ b/include/isocline.h
@@ -333,7 +333,20 @@
 /// Disable or enable multi-line input (enabled by default).
 /// Returns the previous setting.
 bool ic_enable_multiline( bool enable );
+
+/// A callback that decides whether the current `input` is complete.
+/// Return `false` to insert a newline and keep editing instead of accepting
+/// the input when the user presses enter.
+typedef bool (ic_is_complete_fun_t)(const char* input, void* arg);
 
+/// Set a callback that decides when multi-line input is complete.
+/// This lets an application, like a REPL, continue input on a new line for as
+/// long as its own rules consider the input unfinished. There can only be one
+/// such function, setting it again disables the previous one; passing `NULL`
+/// restores the default where enter always accepts the input.
+/// Ignored when multi-line input is disabled.
+void ic_set_is_complete( ic_is_complete_fun_t* is_complete, void* arg );
+
 /// Disable or enable sound (enabled by default).
 /// A beep is used when tab cannot find any completion for example.
 /// Returns the previous setting.
